From 1125ae0b6f40576e5112bcf7e53fafa9f3657bae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 15:02:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: gas interceptor tune from route 00000123 (cap 0.30 +
 panda ceiling, fitted scale/hold offset, engage slew)

Road data (drive-123 report): the 0.15 cap was the binding limit 51% of engaged time; on a ~4% climb the
command sat pinned at 0.15 while the planner asked for +1.0 m/s^2 and speed fell 19.9 -> 17.1 m/s.
Fitted plant aEgo = 2.76*cmd + 0.032 - 0.000935 v^2 - g*pitch (R^2 0.75, 578 bins).

- MAX_INTERCEPTOR_GAS 0.15 -> 0.30 (driver's own p90 pedal on this car; upstream Toyota cap)
- panda: new raw per-track ceiling HYUNDAI_GAS_INTERCEPTOR_MAX_GAS_A/_B = packed 0.30 (1110/559); previously
  any magnitude passed while longitudinal was allowed. Test pins C defines to the packer output.
- PEDAL_SCALE 0.3 -> 0.36 (1/k), HOLD_SPEED_OFFSET refit to measured drag
- upward slew 0.75/s on the pedal command (engage was a 0 -> cap step), lift immediate
- tests: ceiling exact-boundary + per-track, generic sweep replaced with cap-aware one, hill authority,
  hold-speed fit, ramp/lift end-to-end; existing 'gas=1' safety tests now use an in-cap value
